<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 228)</h2>
<p><b>Asobi now cleans up after itself.</b> A storage policy, in three tiers:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Caches evict themselves.</b> Kitsu previews, link downloads and generated slates are capped (10&nbsp;GB by default — Settings ▸ Playback ▸ Downloaded media cap) with the least recently used removed at launch. A <b>Clear Now</b> button empties them on the spot. Link downloads also respect your chosen cache location now.</li>
<li><b>Temp files don't linger.</b> Frames and movies rendered for a Kitsu publish are deleted the moment the upload finishes.</li>
<li><b>Recordings are user data — never silently deleted.</b> Voice notes and session recordings that no saved session references move to the <b>macOS Trash after 30 days</b>, where they stay recoverable. Anything a session mentions is kept regardless of age; anything under 30 days is never touched. Settings ▸ Notes ▸ <b>Housekeeping</b> shows the folder's size, reveals it in Finder, and sweeps orphans on demand.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
